# Throwaway verification scripts — screenshot runs, contrast sweeps,
# the local Tuesday render. They exist for one session and are deleted
# after; this is so a stray one cannot be committed by `git add -A`.
#
# If one of these comes back, it must read the app password from an env
# var. The versions used during the foundation work carried the local
# throwaway password as a string literal, which was safe only because
# they were never committed — that is a property of luck, not design.
.shots.mjs
.verify*.mjs
.tuesday.mjs
.a11y.mjs
.err.mjs
.q.mjs
*.shots.mjs
